# Local-only reference notes (kept on disk, not published)
reference/

# Claude Code local settings (skills are tracked, everything else is local)
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Large local export bundle (frames, uploads, zip) — kept on disk, not published
claude code version/

# npm dependencies
node_modules/

# Python bytecode (generated when skill scripts run)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# motion is vendored into assets/vendor/ so the site has no CDN dependency
node_modules/

# Gallery masters and design frames — build inputs, never served.
#
# tools/prep-gallery.py turns assets/photography and assets/memes into the
# WebP under public/img, and public/img IS committed: the repo already holds
# every byte the site loads, about 2.8MB of it. These are the 30MB of PNG
# behind that, at the SAME 1080x1600 the derivative ships at — lossless copies
# at delivery size, not a higher-resolution archive. Keep them on disk; git
# keeps every version of a binary forever, so 30MB pushed once is 30MB in the
# history for good.
#
# The design frames these were built to are committed, compressed, in
# docs/frames — 212KB for the three of them, which is worth having next to
# docs/outside-work.md since that file argues from them on nearly every page.
assets/photography/
assets/memes/
assets/*.png
